.TH SIGN-IMAGE 1 "October 2026" "scripts" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sign-image \- sign and verify digital images with C2PA Content Credentials
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sign-image
[\fBsign\fR|\fBverify\fR|\fBkeygen\fR] [\fIoptions\fR] \fIfile\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBsign-image\fR embeds tamper-evident cryptographic provenance manifests (C2PA / Content Credentials)
into digital images and multimedia assets (PNG, JPEG, WebP, AVIF, SVG, TIFF).
.PP
The embedded manifest binds the author's declared identity, domain policy, and creation metadata
directly to the SHA-256 hash of the media asset. Any subsequent modification of pixels or metadata
immediately invalidates the provenance signature.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B sign \fR[\fIoptions\fR] \fIfile\fR
Signs an image with C2PA assertions. Automatically generates persistent ES256 signing credentials in
\fB~/.config/nada/c2pa/\fR if no custom key/cert is supplied.
.TP
.B verify \fR[\fB\-\-json\fR] \fIfile\fR
Inspects and verifies the embedded C2PA manifest. Checks pixel hash integrity and reports whether the asset
remains untampered.
.TP
.B keygen \fR[\fB\-d\fR \fIdomain\fR]
Generates or regenerates an ECDSA P-256 (ES256) private key and an X.509 certificate chain.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIpath\fR
Destination path for the signed image (default: \fI<name>_signed.<ext>\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-in-place
Overwrites the source image directly with the signed version.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-title " " \fItitle\fR
Title of the artwork or media file.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-author " " \fIauthor\fR
Author name and contact information (default: \fBDanyaNADAMU <git@nada.mu>\fR).
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-domain " " \fIdomain\fR
Domain name associated with the signer certificate (default: \fBnada.mu\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Prints the full raw C2PA manifest in JSON format when verifying.
.SH AUTHORS
Maintained by DanyaNADAMU <git@nada.mu>.
